jarvis: the Mission Control (local web dashboard)

A single-page mission control served on 127.0.0.1 only - every subsystem
visual and clickable instead of CLI-only. Tabs: Chat (with past sessions),
the Oracle (health screening), the second brain (memory), the kanban board,
watchtower rules, and settings (brain + PRO license activation).

- dashboard.py: local-only HTTP server (port auto-picked from 8773+),
  DashboardState with brain chain + bounded history, JSON API endpoints.
  Lazily imports subsystem modules; settings save preserves a blank key
  field and rebuilds the brain chain; kanban cycling reuses portal.cycle_task.
- dashboard_page.py: single-file HUD client, no external assets.
- cli: jarvis dashboard (LITE - no network exposure, no tool execution).
- Tests: page markers + full server round-trip (page, state, chat,
  memory save/list/forget, kanban add/cycle, watch add/remove, settings
  key preservation, license refusal, 404). Removed a duplicated check
  registration.
- Version 3.2.0.
